<section id="first-discount" class="card" aria-labelledby="first-discount-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="first-discount-heading">FIRST teams — significantly discounted</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>GatherPack started with FIRST, and we want FIRST teams to actually afford managed hosting. Sledgehammer hosts FIRST teams at cost, more or less — a significant discount off the standard tiers. Because program costs vary, we list the philosophy openly but ask you to <a href="/contact/">contact us for the current FIRST rate</a> rather than publishing a stale number.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Proof from the field: <a href="https://westside-robotics.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Westside Robotics</a> and <a href="https://www.team5924.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Golden Gate Robotics</a> shape how we think about build-season costs. See <a href="/use-cases/first-robotics/">FIRST Robotics case →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="what-included" class="card" aria-labelledby="what-included-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="what-included-heading">What’s included (managed)</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <ul class="mb-3">
      <li>All five pillars — <a href="/features/members/">members</a>, <a href="/features/events/">events</a>, <a href="/features/finance/">finance</a>, <a href="/features/communication/">communication</a>, <a href="/features/automation/">automation &amp; reports</a>.</li>
      <li>Hosting, backups, and updates — you manage the organization, not the server.</li>
      <li>Stripe integration for dues/donations; Zeffy/PayPal/Venmo on the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a> as dates land.</li>
      <li>Access to the same MIT source on <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> — no lock-in even when hosted.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-0">Comparing to self-hosting? That table lives on <a href="/open-source/">/open-source</a> as well — same side-by-side, linked both ways.</p>
